module 'MakerPort Network' Comm
author MicroBlocks
version 1 88 
tags network wifi mqtt esp8266 makerport esp 
choices net_connectionMenu 'ESP device' WiFi Internet 'project and group' 
choices net_timezoneMenu UTC 'America/Los_Angeles' 'America/New_York' 'Europe/Berlin' 'Asia/Tokyo' 
choices net_typeMenu number string 
description 'Network communication library for MakerPort with pre-flashed
ESP-01S WiFi module. Sends and receives data via makerbit.com MQTT server.
Compatible with console.makerbit.com and MakerBit devices.

HARDWARE REQUIRED:
  MakerPort with ESP-01S WiFi module connected to serial port:
    MakerPort TX (P18) -> ESP-01S RX
    MakerPort RX (P19) -> ESP-01S TX
    ESP-01S VCC -> 3.3V, GND -> GND

TYPICAL STARTUP SEQUENCE:
  network connect ESP with RX 19 TX 18
  network connect to WiFi "MySSID" password "MyPassword"
  network connect to project "MyProject" and group "MyGroup"
  network wait for connection to [Internet]
  (now ready to send and receive)

CONSOLE:
  Open https://console.makerbit.com in a browser.
  Set Project and Group to match your program.
  Send numbers and strings from the Console; they appear on the MakerPort.
  The MakerPort sends appear in the Console log.

TOPIC FORMAT (internal reference):
  Numbers sent:    pub n_ "value"   or   pub n_channel "value"
  Strings sent:    pub s_ "value"   or   pub s_channel "value"
  Numbers received: n_ value        or   n_channel value
  Strings received: s_ value        or   s_channel value

WIFI SCANNING:
  network scan for WiFi networks
  network wait for WiFi scan to complete for 5000 ms
  repeat (network number of WiFi networks found) [ ... ]
    use (network WiFi network _ name), (network WiFi network _ signal strength),
    (network WiFi network _ is open) to display/choose a network (1 = first found)
  network connect to WiFi (network WiFi network _ name) password (typed or stored password)
  -- or, to auto-pick a network that needs no password:
  network connect to WiFi (network strongest open WiFi network) password (empty text)

TRANSMISSION CONTROL:
  The ESP firmware may have Transmission Control (TC) enabled (default on).
  When TC is active, every ESP->MakerPort message has a trailing 3-digit ID:
    n_ 42 142
    $ESP/connection 3 143
  The MakerPort must reply "ack NNN" for each message received.
  This library handles TC automatically.

IMPORTANT -- line endings:
  The ESP CmdBuffer parser reads incoming serial until LF (byte 10) only.
  Sending CR (byte 13) before LF causes it to appear inside the last parsed
  token, corrupting that parameter (e.g. the WiFi password gets a trailing
  carriage-return and WiFi.begin() fails silently). _net_serialWrite appends
  LF only -- matching the confirmed-working MakeCode reference library.

IMPORTANT -- serial primitives:
  Uses [serial:read] (returns byte array of available bytes).
  Uses [serial:write] (accepts string or byte array).
  Uses [serial:open] baud (MakerPort VM handles P18/P19 automatically).
  Does NOT use [serial:available] or [serial:readByte] (not supported on MakerPort).

CHANGES v1.88:
  - Added WiFi scanning support: network scan for WiFi networks, network WiFi scan
    complete?, network wait for WiFi scan to complete for _ ms, network number of
    WiFi networks found, network WiFi network _ name / signal strength / is open,
    and network strongest open WiFi network. Requires ESP firmware with the new
    "wifi-scan" command (main.cpp CmdCallback bumped from 25 to 26 slots).
    Results are parsed from $ESP/wifi/scan-start, $ESP/wifi/found (quote-delimited
    SSID, since network names may contain spaces), and $ESP/wifi/scan-done.
    Existing net_connectWifi is unchanged -- feed it the scanned network name
    directly (network WiFi network _ name returns a plain string).

CHANGES v1.87:
  - Removed erroneous 0-to-5000 substitution from net_waitFor. The timeout
    value is used as given.

CHANGES v1.86:
  - Fixed net_waitFor timeoutMs not saving: changed spec default from 5000
    to 0. MicroBlocks only saves args that differ from their spec default,
    so any user-entered value is now non-default and persists on save/reload.
    The block treats 0 as 5000 so a freshly placed block still waits 5s.

CHANGES v1.85:
  - Fixed net_waitFor timeout not persisting on save/reload for non-default
    menu choices. MicroBlocks omits trailing arguments that match their
    spec default when saving. Changed menu default to WiFi. Added fallback
    in the block: if timeoutMs arrives as 0 (omitted), substitutes 5000ms.

CHANGES v1.84:
  - Removed || from net_sendNumber and net_sendString spec strings.
    The || expandable-argument syntax renders as visible bars in the block.

CHANGES v1.83:
  - Fixed description string: a single quote inside the v1.81 changelog
    entry was terminating the description early, causing MicroBlocks to
    discard all variables, specs, and blocks when saving to .ubp.

CHANGES v1.82:
  - Fixed _net_processLine assignments for $ESP/tc, $ESP/connection,
    $ESP/error: used local variables to hold the computed value before
    assigning to module variables. Direct assignment of an expression
    followed by return was being mis-serialized by MicroBlocks.

CHANGES v1.81:
  - Fixed _net_processLine: expanded inline single-line if handlers for
    $ESP/tc, $ESP/connection, and $ESP/error into multi-line form matching
    the $ESP/device handler. The inline form was being mis-serialized by
    MicroBlocks as quoted block calls instead of assignments, so
    _net_connection, _net_tcActive, and _net_error were never updated
    from incoming ESP messages.

CHANGES v1.80:
  - Reverted erroneous [serial:open] pin argument change from v1.79.
    MakerPort VM handles P18/P19 automatically; passing pin variables
    as extra arguments broke the net_connectESP block spec.
  - net_lastLine diagnostic reporter remains from v1.7.

CHANGES v1.7:
  - Removed net_sendScreenshot (no LED matrix on MakerPort; block is not
    applicable and was legacy from MakerBit API compatibility).
  - Added net_lastLine reporter: "network last received line". Returns the
    last raw line received from the ESP before parsing. Use during
    diagnostics to confirm what the ESP is actually sending.

CHANGES v1.6:
  - Fixed _net_serialWrite: now sends LF only (byte 10) instead of CR+LF
    (bytes 13, 10). The ESP CmdBuffer parser reads until LF; the preceding
    CR was being included as part of the last parsed token, appending \r to
    the WiFi password (and all other final parameters) and causing WiFi
    connection to fail silently. The MakeCode reference library (confirmed
    working with the same ESP firmware) also sends LF only.
  - Added timeout to net_waitFor: "network wait for connection to [WiFi]
    for [5000] ms". Uses resetTimer/timer primitives. The block returns
    after at most that many milliseconds whether or not the connection
    was made; use net_isConnected to check.

CHANGES v1.3:
  - Reduced compiled size of _net_processLine to avoid "script too large" error.
    Simplified TC detection (replaces 6 unicodeAt calls with split+roundtrip check).
    Extracted date-time parsing into _net_processClock helper.
    Extracted subscription update into _net_updateSub helper.
    All behavior is identical to v1.2.

CHANGES v1.2:
  - Fixed _net_processLine: messages have NO leading ID; topic is first token.
    With TC active, a trailing 3-digit ID is appended after the value.
  - Fixed _net_setMqttApp: now sends "mqtt-app project/group" (single token)
    matching the ESP firmware parser. Previously sent two quoted parameters
    causing the group to be silently dropped and the wrong MQTT topic to be used.
  - Added ACK handling: when TC is active the library now replies "ack NNN"
    for every message received. Without this, the ESP retransmits each message
    20 times then drops the queue with error 70.
  - Fixed net_setTimeZoneOffset / net_setTimeZone: now sends "date-time TZ 600"
    (correct command name and interval). Previously sent "clock TZ" which is not
    a valid ESP command, so time never worked.
  - Fixed _net_normalize: now strips spaces, slashes, and quotes (matching
    MakerBit behavior) instead of replacing them with underscores. This ensures
    MakerPort and MakerBit devices publish to the same MQTT topics.
  - Fixed _net_tzString: now generates POSIX timezone strings accepted by the
    ESP ESPDateTime library (e.g. "<+05:30>-5:30") instead of "UTC+5:30".
  - Fixed net_setTimeZone named zones: converts IANA names to POSIX strings
    matching the MakerBit timezone() helper.
  - Fixed net_connectProject: guards against duplicate subscriptions when called
    more than once.
'
variables _net_rxPin _net_txPin _net_project _net_group _net_connection _net_error _net_device _net_tcActive _net_rxBuf _net_clock_time _net_clock_date _net_clock_weekday _net_clock_tz _net_subscriptions _net_sub_values _net_sub_updated _net_lastLine _net_wifi_names _net_wifi_rssi _net_wifi_open _net_wifi_scanDone 

  spec ' ' 'net_connectGrove' 'network connect ESP to Serial port'
  spec ' ' 'net_connectESP' 'network connect ESP with RX _ TX _' 'num num' 19 18
  spec ' ' 'net_connectWifi' 'network connect to WiFi _ password _' 'str str' 'MyNetwork' 'MyPassword'
  spec ' ' 'net_connectProject' 'network connect to project _ and group _' 'str str' 'MakerPort' '1'
  spec 'r' 'net_isConnected' 'network is connected to _' 'menu.net_connectionMenu' 'WiFi'
  spec ' ' 'net_waitFor' 'network wait for connection to _ for _ ms' 'menu.net_connectionMenu num' 'WiFi' 0
  space
  spec ' ' 'net_scanWifi' 'network scan for WiFi networks'
  spec 'r' 'net_wifiScanDone' 'network WiFi scan complete?'
  spec ' ' 'net_waitForWifiScan' 'network wait for WiFi scan to complete for _ ms' 'num' 5000
  spec 'r' 'net_wifiNetworkCount' 'network number of WiFi networks found'
  spec 'r' 'net_wifiNetworkName' 'network WiFi network _ name' 'num' 1
  spec 'r' 'net_wifiNetworkSignal' 'network WiFi network _ signal strength' 'num' 1
  spec 'r' 'net_wifiNetworkIsOpen' 'network WiFi network _ is open' 'num' 1
  spec 'r' 'net_strongestOpenWifi' 'network strongest open WiFi network'
